From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:21:47 -0500
Subject: feat: a split takes one number, and a pin can take a split

A split is one row, so Cmd-1 to Cmd-9 and the badges count it once: the
number shows on its first pane and the key goes to the pane used last, as
Ctrl-Tab does. A tab that joins a Space pin in a split stays in the pinned run
and is pinned too, so the row is never half a pin, and a drop on a pin's page
now makes that split.

Why: BACKLOG S-102; docs/features/splits.md J2, J3, J5, J13.

Removable when: never as a feature.
